{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats","id":563326,"title":"Alternate to beats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-21T13:17:37-07:00","id":563326,"title":"Alternate to beats?","content":"Love the 2E rules compared to 1E except for 1 thing...beats. I don't like the idea of micromanaging experience when I'm running a game, got too much to think of already. Is there an alternate system anyone uses for experience other than beats? Will there be another optional system in the 2E world of darkness book when it comes out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3137-spiritsponge","name":"SpiritSponge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T13:25:18-07:00","id":563359,"title":"","content":"There's group beats, which you could keep track of by putting pennies or counters in a jar or pile or something. Hit a beat, drop a penny in the jar and keep playing; end of session, distribute the pennies in the jar evenly among the players as beats. That works fine.<br /> <br /> If you find just the act of noticing and adjudicating beats bothersome? For the most part, you can just issue some number of beats, or one experience, or something per session, similarly to issuing experience points in first edition.<br /> <br /> What you want to consider when you do this, though, is how beats factor into certain situations as incentives, specifically those attached to dramatic failures and to Condition resolutions. Some Conditions are more carrot than stick, or even all carrot, like Spooked: their effect is to ask the player to come up with an unwise and risky action in tune with the genre, and lure them with a beat. You could keep these incentives by replacing them with Willpower rewards, which is the general suggestion for quickstarts and NPC resolutions, where beats are not appropriate. Or you could improvise more teeth for these Conditions, granting more situational dice bonuses or penalties as feels fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T13:39:26-07:00","id":563374,"title":"","content":"I don't follow how Beats are micromanaging xp. You could just change the name &quot;Beat&quot; to &quot;experience&quot; and multiply the xp costs of everything by 5. It would then be functionally identical to 1e experience, except without exponentially scaling xp costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T13:55:56-07:00","id":563388,"title":"","content":"I beliebe they mean the fact that you handle Beats during the game acording to certain events as oposed of giving experiences at the end of the sesion. Some people may find that that breaks the flow of or slows down the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T14:28:57-07:00","id":563414,"title":"","content":"Oh, ok. I see how that could be an issue. You could just award a set number of Beats or Experiences per session. Then have the things that normally grant Beats during play grant Willpower instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:01:11-07:00","id":563429,"title":"","content":"Aren't you just &quot;micromanaging&quot; willpower instead then?<br /> <br /> Seriously though how are beats any different from the other potential rewards for doing stuff? Health, willpower, energy points, integrity analogue, It's just one extra thing to keep track of on the sheet. Why would that break the flow any more than everything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:50:25-07:00","id":563461,"title":"","content":"I don't personally have an issue with beats, but I've known several people who do. One fought tooth and nail to try and get me to use a house rule that I've seen fairly often other places (though I don't think I've seen it here).<br /> <br /> The house rule I usually see is: 1 xp per session, and any beats earned are used for rerolls instead.<br /> <br /> Of course, then you're still &quot;micromanaging&quot; beats, but if you do the suggestion of just chucking a poker chip or whatever at players when they earn one, it's really not that bad.<br /> <br /> The player in my group that wanted this was also somewhat satisfied with group beats as a compromise, though I think his concern was more deviating power levels (the beat system can very easily allow a player to get way more than others).<br /> <br /> For me, personally? Before I switched to Group Beats (which seem to work wonderfully), I just did all the beats at the end and told my players that if they forgot something, that's on them. The Storyteller shouldn't be expected to remember everything about the players' sheets. I also leave them in charge of reminding me about their Masks/Dirges and Aspirations, though I suspect most people would disagree with that decision. With Group Beats, I just follow the &quot;chuck it in a pile&quot; method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","user":"Maina","date":". 06-21-2015, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:20:50-07:00","id":563508,"title":"","content":"That's my problem. I simply won't catch or remember every time they should've gotten a beat. It would be easier just to reward experience at the end of the session based on their roleplaying, furthering of the story, etc. I guess I could use the 1e experience system and give beats out that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3137-spiritsponge","name":"SpiritSponge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T17:26:21-07:00","id":563570,"title":"","content":"Two solutions. One? Stop trying to remember on your part, Spirit. Put that all on the players' heads. Trust me, if they want EXP, then they'll remember.<br /> <br /> Two, don't say &quot;Take a beat.&quot; Get some little poker chips, beads, anything physical to hand out during the game. Having something tangible in hand actually increases the excitement a lot. It also allows for more non-verbal communication at the table when they want a beat by pointing at it the beat tokens instead of interrupting play. <br /> <br /> <br /> As for completely removing it? I'm not sure. Beats are pretty critical for the entire Condition system, and that's a cornerstone of how 2e plays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:38:55-07:00","id":563621,"title":"","content":"My players mostly keep track of their own beats. They can ask me if I think something is deserving of a beat, such as whether a given scene really furthered an Aspiration of theirs. They also keep track of their Mask/Dirge and ask me for confirmation when they think they should get Willpower. I don't have to micromanage anything.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't <i>want </i>to micromanage those things. The players, on the other hand, enjoy taking those things into their own hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T19:09:44-07:00","id":563639,"title":"","content":"I've never had trouble tracking Beats, but I use a lot of manipulatives during play. I've got bags full of those little glass bead things with the flat bottoms in lots of different colors (blue for Willpower, red for Vitae, black for Beats, etc.), stacks of Condition cards, and a few other odds and ends. So, when a character gains a Condition, I hand them a Condition card. When they resolve it, they hand the card back to me and I hand them a black bead. When a player rolls a failure, they can tell me if they want to make it a dramatic failure and I hand them a black bead. When a player feels they've fulfilled one of their Aspirations, they say so and I either agree and hand them a black bead or disagree and tell them what they need to do next to fulfill it. When a player frenzies, I hand them a black bead. Etc. Whenever a player accumulates five black beads, they hand them back to me and write their exp on their character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T03:58:53-07:00","id":563940,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's the best way to do it in my opinion. I mean, experience and Beats are the rewards to players, they want them and will keep track of when they are suposed to be awarded one. I suggest using the Group Beats option, I have found that increases the cohesion of the group, players going out of their way to help one another fullfill Aspirations and so on. Makes it a lot easier to involve the rest of the group on the personal subplots of the other characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T09:23:18-07:00","id":564187,"title":"","content":"I normaly hink that a players hunt for &quot;juice&quot; or willpower is mostly a bit more micromanaging and even metagaming than beats, because players normally need mostly a quick fix of juice or wp - beats or xp are just the cherry atop the cupcake after the game. normally any xp-expenditure is regulated to the end of the session. <br /> As written above by Charlaquin: quintuple the xp-cost of everything and beats are now simple xp points. there is no need for an xp-subsystem called beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T09:24:39-07:00","id":564188,"title":"","content":"I love the new second edition rules as well. However I hate beats and I hate writing down aspirations. I feel the beats reward your character for failures and not for doing a good job. It is too easy to manipulate and make your character terrible in order to just gain beat after beat after beat for dramatic failures? Go off and do stupid things and make poor choices just to get that beat. Try to get as many conditions as I can just so I can resolve them for that beat. To me... and this might be Only me and I am ok with that... To me it just feels like it takes away from the roleplaying because now you are making out of character choices that influence your in character choices. I am no longer thinking &quot;would my character honestly do that?&quot; I am thinking &quot;lets make it dramatic screw up so I can get that beat&quot;<br /> <br /> I have used them though. When I tried to do it, I felt i spent more time on handing them out and handing out cards or asking players &quot;do you want a dramatic&quot; and it took away from the game. When I handed it over to the players it did go a lot better. When I did a beat bowl with beads it went even more smoothly. Trial and error. I did have my players just tossing in beads and tell me on their own to make it a dramatic failure. which helped immensely with the flow of the game. However almost all of my players enjoy the strict role playing aspect a lot more than worry about beats. We do still play with conditions and whatnot for the roleplaying vs mechanical aspect. I usually give out 1-2 exp per game session based on things similar to beats. Were my players ready/on time/prepared? Did the Role play all their conditions? Did they make choices based on what their characters would do? Were the objectives resolved (group aspirations so to speak)? Did my players complete their personal goals (or aspirations) ?<br /> <br /> When I do a beat bowl. it usually ends up being 1-2 exp anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T09:29:16-07:00","id":564191,"title":"","content":"Have you never heard of learning from your mistakes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T09:51:32-07:00","id":564205,"title":"","content":"And Beats should be awarded for dramatic situations arising from those failures, not just any screw up, especially if the players are failing on purpose and acting stupid to farm experiences. You are the final arbiter on what deserves to be awarded a Beat and not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T10:01:14-07:00","id":564211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=564188#post564188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the new second edition rules as well. However I hate beats and I hate writing down aspirations. I feel the beats reward your character for failures and not for doing a good job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think these two things are a bit related.<br /> <br /> Aspirations reward you beats for doing well. The dramatic failure option exists for making your failures more interesting. There's also a reason why we have people running the game. As a ST, I would never allow a player to just shop around for inconsequential rolls to fail and take a &quot;dramatic&quot; failure with no real consequences for a Beat.<br /> <br /> Conditions are a mix. Most Conditions are negative, but there are positive ones as well, they reward you either way. And many negative ones can still be the result of &quot;doing a good job.&quot; As your characters advance in XP, they'll have a much easier time generating positive Conditions on themselves and others, providing a greater feeling of &quot;reward for doing well,&quot; on top of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T11:09:16-07:00","id":564327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=564191#post564191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you never heard of learning from your mistakes?</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is directed at me... It's rude. There is no explaination on what you mean at all. Did you read the post in it's entirety? We tried several different methods and found what worked best with our group. essentailly... we learned from OUR mistakes and moved on to have a great time. I was simply offering my opinion on beats, I was not intending on starting a hate war. Offer constructive criticism or dont post.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=564205#post564205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Beats should be awarded for dramatic situations arising from those failures, not just any screw up, especially if the players are failing on purpose and acting stupid to farm experiences. You are the final arbiter on what deserves to be awarded a Beat and not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with you. 100% which is why our group as a whole chose to do a beat bowl one game and simply just give out the average for the remainder of the chronicle. Rules as written however dont give a difference on if the player is farming or actually... just playing. Unless i am wrong it says you get a beat for a dramatic failure. and I have played in a few online groups where people took a dramatic on every fail they got simply for the beat, which is where most of my distain has come from. I think players should get also rewarded for doing amazing things, creative thinking, exploring new unique avenues. The beat system does not allow for that in anyway. What if a player got 10 successses on something or had an amazing idea that saved the group from certain death? Sure i can hand out beats, but. Rules as written. that would not apply. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=564211#post564211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think these two things are a bit related.<br /> <br /> Aspirations reward you beats for doing well. The dramatic failure option exists for making your failures more interesting. There's also a reason why we have people running the game. As a ST, I would never allow a player to just shop around for inconsequential rolls to fail and take a &quot;dramatic&quot; failure with no real consequences for a Beat.<br /> <br /> Conditions are a mix. Most Conditions are negative, but there are positive ones as well, they reward you either way. And many negative ones can still be the result of &quot;doing a good job.&quot; As your characters advance in XP, they'll have a much easier time generating positive Conditions on themselves and others, providing a greater feeling of &quot;reward for doing well,&quot; on top of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes they are related in the sense that you get a beat for completing an aspiration. And as a story teller I dont let people shop for beats either. Which is why i dislike them because it is soooo so so easy to &quot;farm&quot; with the rules as they are written. It is so easy for players to have aspirations that are ... for lack of a better word right now.... Lame. Every good character has a personal agenda. Goals they want to reach. Things they want to do. I am just saying that aspirations are also way too easy to manipulate to just farm beats again. Or things that will never come up in the course of the game. I had a player tell me his character's dream goal was to have a 3 way with a vampire and a werewolf and he was human... No matter how many times I told him that was entirely unlikely...he insisted. It was within his rights and I should cater to it... <br /> <br /> Off the top of my head. Inspired and steadfast dont offer beats. Those are two of the positive conditions that you get for doing a good job. I do understand there are other conditions. <br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps I have not had a good string of online games. Perhaps I have encountered far too much &quot;farming of beats&quot; As a story teller ... Which is what the point of this entire thread was.. i was simply offering an alternative to the usage of beats and supporting my reasons for suggesting it. I did read in earlier posts that others also just used a blanket 1exp per game session. I find this reasonable. Fair and quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T11:28:14-07:00","id":564354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=564327#post564327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If this is directed at me... It's rude. There is no explaination on what you mean at all. Did you read the post in it's entirety? We tried several different methods and found what worked best with our group. essentailly... we learned from OUR mistakes and moved on to have a great time. I was simply offering my opinion on beats, I was not intending on starting a hate war. Offer constructive criticism or dont post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I chose to interpret Elfive's statement as a rationale of why you get beats for failures (learning from mistakes), and not as a personal attack. But I agree it could be interpreted either way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=564327#post564327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I have not had a good string of online games. Perhaps I have encountered far too much &quot;farming of beats&quot; As a story teller ... Which is what the point of this entire thread was.. i was simply offering an alternative to the usage of beats and supporting my reasons for suggesting it. I did read in earlier posts that others also just used a blanket 1exp per game session. I find this reasonable. Fair and quick.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a storyteller I would, just as others recommended, just disallow the farming of beats. I know the books could have been more explicit, but beats are meant for dramatic situations with consequences. Vampire hides this info under the Resisting Frenzy header on p.104, for example.<br /> <br /> I really hope the writers clarify this in the new WoD 2nd edition book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 06-22-2015, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T11:30:59-07:00","id":564357,"title":"","content":"I meant that common wisdom is that you can gain experience by messing up. Like what the beat system models. Sorry if that was unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T11:44:23-07:00","id":564374,"title":"","content":"Vitalis is saying exactly what I've been thinking about the beat system. I can already see the players abusing the system just to gain beats. Dramatic failures will constantly come up just so they can gain a beat making the characters look like a bunch of bungling idiots and ruin a serious campaign. I want the characters to play the game instead of always thinking how they will get their next beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3137-spiritsponge","name":"SpiritSponge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:17:55-07:00","id":564428,"title":"","content":"Reading all those posts about players potentially abusing the system makes me feel blessed to have my group of story-focussed players, who believe that rules as intended are more important than rules as written, and that mechanics should serve the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:19:17-07:00","id":564431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpiritSponge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=564374#post564374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I can already see the players abusing the system just to gain beats.</div> </div> </div> </div> The issue is that's not a bug of the system, its a feature. There's a limit to how many beats you can get a scene,but the idea behind it is that you're supposed to &quot;abuse&quot; it. That's doing it right. <br /> <br /> If anything, I'm of the opinion that those who are laid back and not very forceful gamers are going to end up in the back behind everyone else, which might be an issue. But so-called abuse is working as intended.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:26:46-07:00","id":564436,"title":"","content":"No experience system is going to fix a group where the players are out to game the system for as much experience as possible and the GM is out to thwart them. The Beat system is predicated on all parties playing in good faith. If you are worried about players not playing in good faith, you should talk to your players about that. Now, in that conversation you may very well decide that the Beat system is not for you, and that's fine. I stand by my recommendation to award a fixed number of Beats/experiences per session and award Willpower or something for the things that normally award Beats, if you do find that your group doesn't like the Beat system. But when I hear someone say they don't like the system because it's too easy to earn experiences by doing stupid things on purpose, I can't help but feel the problem is not the system but the group dynamic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:46:01-07:00","id":564451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=564431#post564431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The issue is that's not a bug of the system, its a feature. There's a limit to how many beats you can get a scene,but the idea behind it is that you're supposed to &quot;abuse&quot; it. That's doing it right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just searched the second edition books for this beats per scene limit, but could not find it. I think it is only mentioned in the God Machine Chronicle.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I wanted to say that I agree with Charlaquin's post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:56:22-07:00","id":564465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpiritSponge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=564374#post564374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dramatic failures will constantly come up just so they can gain a beat making the characters look like a bunch of bungling idiots and ruin a serious campaign. I want the characters to play the game instead of always thinking how they will get their next beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth highlighting that you can only take the beat to dramatically fail a roll you were failing anyway. You're not trading success for dramatic failure, you're trading failure for dramatic failure. As the ST you have a huge amount of control over how a dramatic failure plays out. There are lots of tools and options, which means you have a lot of ways to avoid them looking incompetent. They don't even need to see some of them (for example a NPC gaining a positive Condition against the PCs isn't exactly &quot;visible&quot; to them). As long as the results make sense as something that could have happened anyway, it's easy to mix personal failures with external failures to avoid the &quot;bungling idiots&quot; effect.<br /> <br /> And the players are supposed to work on getting beats. That's why beats come from the sources they do. Setting and fulfilling goals, resolving Conditions, taking dramatic failures, good RP... these are all things the players should basically be doing anyway. It's what they should be thinking about, which is, &quot;what should my character be doing that advances the plot or is at least making the story more interesting?&quot; Because that's what gets you beats.<br /> <br /> There isn't really an issue with &quot;gaming&quot; a system intended to be gamed. The potential issue is players rejecting the spirit of the rules (&quot;make things more fun/interesting and get a reward&quot;) and just focus on the reward. But then you get to Charlaquin's point about this needing to be a talk with the group; not a rules issue.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T13:06:54-07:00","id":564476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=564436#post564436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But when I hear someone say they don't like the system because it's too easy to earn experiences by doing stupid things on purpose, I can't help but feel the problem is not the system but the group dynamic.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> If certain group members seem to be abusing/farming or whatever you want to call it (They technically are playing it the way the rule book says), and leaving the rest of the group behind, maybe they don't belong with that group. (Not to ostracize or anything, just that they might enjoy being in a group with like-minded individuals. Unless they prefer being the higher exp character in the chronicle without being an NPC or something)<br /> <br /> I also completely agree with some others, let the group take care of their beats. Like others have said, if they want the exp, they will remember it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T13:10:04-07:00","id":564479,"title":"","content":"I've been playing RPGs with the same group for many years and everyone of them are experienced players. They get into some serious role playing and intrigue but will also use the rules to their advantage and they have every right to. The group dynamic is fine it's the rules that are in question this time. I just think 1e got it right over 2e when it comes to experience. Other than that I think 2e is better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3137-spiritsponge","name":"SpiritSponge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T16:24:56-07:00","id":564726,"title":"","content":"Um. As said before, you're trading a failure for a dramatic failure. It's not really any more bumbling than it would be otherwise.<br /> <br /> Perhaps more importantly, dramatic failure doesn't have to be a failure on the character's part. Read the example dramatic failures. They can be external things that mess up the characters' plans further. An example is the dramatic failure of Mesmerize, where your target is so much stronger of will than you that they are empowered by their ability to resist. It isn't that the vampire is a bumbling fool, but that their target is a paragon of mental strength, at least in that moment.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if I have a character trying to pick a lock and they dramatic fail, I might not have them break their picks and scream in surprise like a fool. I might just have it be that the 'dramatic failure' means that they can hear a guard patrol coming down the corridor just this moment by chance, so they have to go hide and/or find another way in. They've failed and they cannot continue to roll, but that doesn't make them bumbling fools.<br /> <br /> 2e rewards players for allowing interesting obstacles and complications to be injected into the story. It only rewards the players for acting like bumbling idiots if you interpret a failure as the result of being an idiot. Sometimes things just don't work out, even after you do everything right. That applies IC as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T09:31:39-07:00","id":565485,"title":"","content":"If SpiritSponge's crew is already embracing the game's drama/politics, and playing up negative conditions without meta-incentives, then they're right - beats aren't a necessary factor for that campaign.<br /> <br /> If a crew tends to try to maximize their successes and avoid hardship/drama in most situations, beats are a good way to start teaching them that setbacks can also be a compelling aspect to the game. If a crew has a hard time coming to terms with their characters being Mesmerized or Possessed or any of the conditions which have historically been seen as 'removing protagonism' then again, beats are a way to incentivize players to break out of that comfort zone.<br /> <br /> I was worried about the Dramatic Failure clause for a recent game I started, partially because of the possible 'Keystone Kindred' effect, but also because the gaming experience between the players was going to be very different (one first-timer, one average, one ten year vet). I chose to go with group beats and that seems to have encouraged the crew to help each other with aspirations. But I also started with the Dramatic Failure option in my hands as the ST.<br /> <br /> Rather than just let the players declare they want the Dramatic Failure, I offer it during appropriate moments/rolls in a narrative way. For example, when trying to stealth into an old factory they blew the roll and I announced, &quot;Just as you rush across the street, headlights flare on in the parking garage across from you. Is it a normal failure and there's just been a witness to someone sneaking into the factory who might turn over info to a later investigation, or is it a dramatic failure and you just got spotted by a patrol car that's going to start heading your way?&quot;<br /> <br /> To second what Maina said, I tend to frame the Dramatic Failure as turns of circumstance rather than, &quot;You trip and fall as you run across the street and bash your head on the concrete.&quot; There's a difference between unexpected complications you have to deal with and you just looking stupid as a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T19:09:20-07:00","id":567238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=563388#post563388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe they mean the fact that you handle Beats during the game according to certain events as opposed of giving experiences at the end of the session. Some people may find that that breaks the flow of or slows down the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the problem. Other game systems have been giving in session experience for decades.<br /> Hell Chaosium , one of the oldest game systems out there has had skill checks since the beginning. You marked those as you got them.<br /> <br /> I don't like group xp. It feels like social promotion to me. Why should someone who doesn't really do anything other than show up and not engage in the game get the same reward as everyone else?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T23:38:20-07:00","id":567464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=567238#post567238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like group xp. It feels like social promotion to me. Why should someone who doesn't really do anything other than show up and not engage in the game get the same reward as everyone else?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only time I've really seen people not engage at a private tabletop game are when a significant other gets brought along who is more interested in spending time with their partner as opposed to the game itself. Otherwise, people usually want to engage but don't necessarily know how, either because of rules ignorance, because of newness to the group, because of a softer personality, etc.<br /> <br /> Group beats have actually been a boon for me in helping those softer type of players <i>get</i> engaged. The proactive, aggressive, advancement-minded role-player can be gung ho about collecting their beats pretty quickly, and its a great incentive for them. Group beats switch that advancement incentive from &quot;Let me do all these things to get my beats and then step out of the way&quot; to &quot;Every time a beat is given, 1/xth of it is mine.&quot;<br /> <br /> I've enjoyed seeing those active players realize that it is both mechanically strategic AND dramatically interesting to get the more passive players to collect their beats, so it keeps them invested in the group dynamic. It also allows them to act as a mentor or sounding board for fulfilling aspirations, conditions or taking dramatic failures when they might hesitate to go out on a limb on their own.<br /> <br /> Obviously if a player is truly being a bump-on-the-log do-nothing type, that's not good. And yes, you don't want to necessarily reward people for actually doing nothing. I guess I just don't see those types of players much outside of LARP or pickup games where I probably wouldn't use group beats, or beats at all (LARP).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T14:39:52-07:00","id":586445,"title":"","content":"My group has abandoned Aspirations altogether. They were taking between thirty and forty minutes each session for people to rework them, and most of the time the game would go in it's own direction. To get the beats the players ended up either having to yank the rest of the group into some situation and away from the current crisis, or the game turned into a round robin session of one-on-one RPG sessions as people rush around trying to get their beats in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5995-jonwake","name":"JonWake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5995_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T15:10:03-07:00","id":586471,"title":"","content":"Group Beats have been wonderful in my groups games, we found when we were not using them that the players who were more adept at going after their goals got more beats and it got a bit insane, also it was often difficult to remember when you should get a beat or not, having a bin where everyone puts a beat into when they get it has made it easier (aside form the inevitable blowup if someone seems o fish around as a player worries about jiggery pokey... but thats neither here nor there)<br /> <br /> As to aspirations, I have one very important piece of advice, remember that they are not &quot;Character aspirations&quot; but &quot;Player aspirations&quot; they are the key method used to tell a storyteller the things you are looking forward to in game and the types of stories you are trying to tell. At the beginning of game i ask all my players their aspirations and write them down, Then usually i take a few moments to bounce those off of my general plan for the story and see which branches hold up best.<br /> <br /> As to writing Aspirations, Be very generic, give the ST'er as much room as possible For Example, in a WtF game I was playing, i had my aspirations in my head, and was writing them down, one was to find the werewolf that we had fought with at the edge of our territory the game before, but as the hammer was swinging down, i wrote for my aspiration &quot;Find Werewolf&quot; the game shifted tone and we spent an amount of time in the Hisil fighting an owl spirit that had waylaid me earlier, and never even started looking for that werewolf, however, on the way, we ran into a friendly pack from a different border, I double-checked at the end of game with the story-teller (we hold aspirations until the end of the chapter, which makes it a bit easier and helps do a quick run-down of what was accomplished and keeps us from pausing game) and he said, well yeah, you did &quot;Find werewolf&quot; even if not the one you were looking for...<br /> <br /> Remember, Player Advancement is not a bad thing to a chronicle, Reward players for good roleplaying sessions, Aspirations and beats make this a way that you can bring players into the story and move the action along, not hinder it.<br /> <br /> Tl;Dr:<br /> Group Beats<br /> General Player Aspirations<br /> Be Broad in Apsirations<br /> Get Beats Build Experiences,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T15:25:28-07:00","id":586484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hackthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=586471#post586471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tl;Dr:<br /> Group Beats<br /> General Player Aspirations<br /> Be Broad in Apsirations<br /> Get Beats Build Experiences,</div> </div> </div> </div>Profit<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Sorry, I had too.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T15:26:19-07:00","id":586486,"title":"","content":"So, I've recently run into a situation where I'm not sure Beats will be appropriate for a game I'll be running. I've got a group of new players (one has played a little bit of D&amp;D before, but they're all very new to RPGs), who are very excited to try a one-shot paranormal investigation game for Halloween, so I've agreed to run a short WoD story for them. If they enjoy it, there is a possibility of some or all of them continuing as a more regular group, so I'll be including some seeds for a longer chronicle in this first adventure, but still writing it to be a satisfying and complete experience on its own.<br /> <br /> The problem is, what to do about Beats? Since this may or may not end up being a one and done game, there's no guarantee their Beats will ever be useful to them. I could award Willpower instead, but as new players I'm not sure if they'll find that appealing enough to want to resolve things like Shaken and Spooked. Any ideas? Anyone else have experience running one-shot stories in 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T15:34:33-07:00","id":586503,"title":"","content":"Maybe give them a small list of merits to choose from per character, and then use beats but allow them the second they get 5 beats buy one of the merits? It depends somewhat on how long of a session you are planning, but if your story would/could grant more than a whole experience a player, you can show off a bit of the advancement section which usually will grab gamers by the nose and have them follow the direction you want them to go :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T08:50:26-07:00","id":587172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hackthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=586503#post586503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe give them a small list of merits to choose from per character, and then use beats but allow them the second they get 5 beats buy one of the merits? It depends somewhat on how long of a session you are planning, but if your story would/could grant more than a whole experience a player, you can show off a bit of the advancement section which usually will grab gamers by the nose and have them follow the direction you want them to go :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I like that idea. Maybe give a little disclaimer that normally I'd have them spend experiences between sessions, but since this is going to be a short game I'll let them spend it right away to get a taste for how advancement works. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T21:51:02-08:00","id":1191834,"title":"","content":"I also think that the Beats system is awful. Terrible idea. Too much micromanage and too much metagaming in the aspirations. Just use the old system but give beats instead of EXP points, because the stats are flat now, no longer current rating x n. So you need to give less experience per game<br /> <br /> One note, the statement that &quot;giving beats for dramatic failure is to be an incentive to players to make their failures dramatic&quot; is complete BS! This is just a workaround of the system to allow dramatic failures to simply happen! Otherwise, it would be very rare, you have to have zero dice pool to have a dramatic failure. White Wolf always were very bad at system design. Wonderful stories and settings, but terrible systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12056-zulmaran","name":"Zulmaran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12056_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T07:22:58-08:00","id":1191916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpiritSponge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats#post563326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love the 2E rules compared to 1E except for 1 thing...beats. I don't like the idea of micromanaging experience when I'm running a game, got too much to think of already. Is there an alternate system anyone uses for experience other than beats? Will there be another optional system in the 2E world of darkness book when it comes out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just give 1-2 XP per session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T07:36:56-08:00","id":1191921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zulmaran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1191834#post1191834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that the Beats system is awful. Terrible idea. Too much micromanage and too much metagaming in the aspirations. Just use the old system but give beats instead of EXP points, because the stats are flat now, no longer current rating x n. So you need to give less experience per game<br /> <br /> One note, the statement that &quot;giving beats for dramatic failure is to be an incentive to players to make their failures dramatic&quot; is complete BS! This is just a workaround of the system to allow dramatic failures to simply happen! Otherwise, it would be very rare, you have to have zero dice pool to have a dramatic failure. White Wolf always were very bad at system design. Wonderful stories and settings, but terrible systems.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think their system is just fine with a few minor tweaks. I agree that beats are terrible and it takes too much micromanaging and there is too much metagaming. And if you have someone particularly inclined... they just abuse the system entirely and suddenly they have like 100 beats for really stupid shit..<br /> <br /> <br /> I am with Gallus. As long as my players progressed the story, I give 1-2 EXP per session played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T03:10:06-08:00","id":1192187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=587172#post587172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I like that idea. Maybe give a little disclaimer that normally I'd have them spend experiences between sessions, but since this is going to be a short game I'll let them spend it right away to get a taste for how advancement works. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>For One-Shots, I really liked that earlier suggestion about Beats being gained and spent to re-roll dice. It's a powerful commodity, then.<br /> <br /> In addition, I never liked Beats and gaining EXP in general for One-Shots. It always seemed easier to have loosely planned 'intervals' in the narrative when you either give the group a set amount of EXP to spend in the case of time lapses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T04:01:52-08:00","id":1192194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1191921#post1191921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think their system is just fine with a few minor tweaks. I agree that beats are terrible and it takes too much micromanaging and there is too much metagaming. And if you have someone particularly inclined... they just abuse the system entirely and suddenly they have like 100 beats for really stupid shit..<br /> <br /> <br /> I am with Gallus. As long as my players progressed the story, I give 1-2 EXP per session played.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the old ways were better. In the last session, i forgot that every time a vampire in Requiem Frenzys, it gets a beat. So, i missed a lot of beats for my player. Also, as soon as they realized this, they try all the time to frenzy when it's convenient, for example, in a fight when they are sure they will win, etc. Its just terrible. And my god the conditions..... terrible terrible ideas.<br /> <br /> About the systems, i also thought like you before, but once you taste the better refined and created systems, its hard to look back. I know people will get on me for this, but GURPS is excellent. Everything works there, the system is very thought out and constructed. We still play with white wolf systems because its just easier to start up a game instead of adapting all the rules. But do take a look, just for curiosity on Vampire The Masquerade/Werewolf etc. for GURPS and you will see that all the problems of those games were solved there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12056-zulmaran","name":"Zulmaran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12056_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T06:00:51-08:00","id":1192217,"title":"","content":"That's is hardly a problem of the system and all a fault of the players and Storyteller. No rule survives contatc with what amounts to douches.If they want to game the system they will, no matter what the system is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T09:04:12-08:00","id":1192278,"title":"","content":"simple rule - beat is only generated if the source enhances the story <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If people are gonna start abusing frenzies just to get the beats - don't give them.<br /> Or if they still want it - create complications. You just frenzied in combat for a Beat? Oh, look some innocent by standards come along. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T09:24:52-08:00","id":1192287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192217#post1192217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's is hardly a problem of the system and all a fault of the players and Storyteller. No rule survives contatc with what amounts to douches.If they want to game the system they will, no matter what the system is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is it a douche if it's within the rules? I mean the rules say that you get a beat every time you frenzy, so why NOT frenzy all the time? You get a beat every time you go get a fix ( addicted ) instead of doing what the story teller says? Why not go wrack up the beats and deal with the story later? Short term aspiration, I want to go get a big mac. Done. Beat. Now I want to eat it. Done. Beat. Now I want to drive to my sister's. Done. Beat. Now she wants to get a big mac, Done. Beat.<br /> <br /> Ok So that's a little extreme, but within the rules. Sure people will power game and Min/max, but the beat system opened the door and said, come on in! Just take the beats out and people will make better choices because the cheese isnt there to cheese it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T09:39:51-08:00","id":1192294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192287#post1192287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok So that's a little extreme, but within the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is playing a mortals game and sticking a fork in an electrical socket every session to get the Beat for having your righmost Health boxes marked. The game is written to incentivize players to have their characters make otherwise &quot;bad&quot; decisions under the assumption that everyone involved is capable of being a mature adult that can communicate and collaborate.<br /> <br /> Entering frenzy requires failing the roll and going along with directives that are usually a bad idea in the immediate term, and steering that to a different goal requires risking any failure locking you into that state until you lose Humanity \u2014 a state that the game <i>also</i> encourages you to move toward by giving you a Beat for rolling to avoid losing Humanity and for turning a failure into a dramatic failure. Are you going to argue that every vampire immediately succumbs to long-term frenzy as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T12:49:22-08:00","id":1192353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192294#post1192294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is playing a mortals game and sticking a fork in an electrical socket every session to get the Beat for having your righmost Health boxes marked. The game is written to incentivize players to have their characters make otherwise &quot;bad&quot; decisions under the assumption that everyone involved is capable of being a mature adult that can communicate and collaborate.<br /> <br /> Entering frenzy requires failing the roll and going along with directives that are usually a bad idea in the immediate term, and steering that to a different goal requires risking any failure locking you into that state until you lose Humanity \u2014 a state that the game <i>also</i> encourages you to move toward by giving you a Beat for rolling to avoid losing Humanity and for turning a failure into a dramatic failure. Are you going to argue that every vampire immediately succumbs to long-term frenzy as well?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say you can choose to fail the frenzy roll. ( you can't choose to go into a frenzy whenever you want unless you have the required things. ) however it's like choosing to fail anything else you just dont fight the beast. Like someone else pointed out, if you're winning the battle, you dont really need to frenzy, but they choose to just to get the beat. likely they have taken damage and that is enough to provoke a frenzy check...<br /> <br /> The beat system encourages stupidity and failure as it is. That is what I was saying. That is what I was agreeing with. The beat system should encourage success and exceptional ideas and creativity, not just favoring the fuck ups. <br /> <br /> Why would I be a more experienced mortal for sticking a fork in the electrical socket than the person who made good choices by getting out there and being 'exceptional' ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T13:17:49-08:00","id":1192363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192353#post1192353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say you can choose to fail the frenzy roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanics don't work that way, much like how you can't just voluntarily fail a Harmony breaking point in Werewolf. You wanna frenzy on purpose? Ride the wave and take the gamble that that failure brings to bear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The beat system encourages stupidity and failure as it is. That is what I was saying. That is what I was agreeing with. The beat system should encourage success and exceptional ideas and creativity, not just favoring the fuck ups. </div> </div> </div>The system for a storytelling game covering ostensibly dramatic narratives meant to show off the characters' strengths <i>and weaknesses</i> does not need to encourage players to try to do well, because doing well is already the victory condition.<br /> <br /> &quot;Exceptional ideas and creativity&quot; are not quantified by the mechanics in any more meaningful way than fiat, and if they were then you would be running into the same issue you're bringing up now except with &quot;stupidity&quot; replaced by &quot;checklist mentality.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would I be a more experienced mortal for sticking a fork in the electrical socket than the person who made good choices by getting out there and being 'exceptional' ? </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't, any more than you would be a more experienced vampire for frenzying constantly. You don't get a Beat for every roll you fail, period, you get a Beat for <i>inviting complications into the story</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>What you will be</i>, provided you lean as hard as possible into Beat criteria, is <i>playing with higher stakes than the characters who take it slow.</i> A vampire who frenzies constantly becomes a larger threat more rapidly and finds themselves in danger more frequently. Beats make that mode of play <i>a tempting thing to dip into</i>. Most vampires will not frenzy constantly and feed beyond their capacity on the regular, because their society and basic forethought recognizes the trajectory of committing to that behavioral arc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T14:00:20-08:00","id":1192383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192217#post1192217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's is hardly a problem of the system and all a fault of the players and Storyteller. No rule survives contatc with what amounts to douches.If they want to game the system they will, no matter what the system is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree completely. If a system is faulty, the player will abuse it. If its not, the player won't be able to. Its like saying that its the players fault if the video game your are playing has low security and allows hacks, because they shouldn't abuse it. No way, the fault is with the game, that didn't plan on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12056-zulmaran","name":"Zulmaran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12056_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T14:08:50-08:00","id":1192386,"title":"","content":"The point is, even if i put a passerby in the frenzy moment, i will have to do that everytime someone tries to frenzy on purpose. Besides, this only creates more discussion at the table, some player may think they are being treated unfairly, like im keeping them from earning beats. Thats why im against this idea that you earn experience from failures IN GAMES. If its this way, it should only be used if the failure is random, not by player control.<br /> Even in GURPS, there are people who buy disadvantages in the hopes that they are never brought up. But there is easier to control because its happening before the game starts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12056-zulmaran","name":"Zulmaran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12056_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T14:10:44-08:00","id":1192388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zulmaran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192383#post1192383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree completely. If a system is faulty, the player will abuse it. If its not, the player won't be able to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wordcount is a thing, and the amount of words necessary to make system abuse even remotely close to impossible is a prohibitively large allotment to make under the assumption of an adversarial playstyle being the norm for a game you are ostensibly playing with friends for fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its like saying that its the players fault if the video game your are playing has low security and allows hacks, because they shouldn't abuse it. No way, the fault is with the game, that didn't plan on this. </div> </div> </div>You're not playing a video game. Video games have the inimitable resource of &quot;the setting and mechanics are fixed in place unless you alter the game from outside.&quot; TTRPGs are run entirely by people who don't have to render a new environment in detail if they want to go off the defined path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T14:37:56-08:00","id":1192400,"title":"","content":"At the risk of threadcapping (does it even apply to necroed ones like this?), I must exclaim,<br /> <br /> Not this again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T14:50:16-08:00","id":1192406,"title":"","content":"I see your point Satchel, but even so, there are systems that are more open to abuse than others. This one is. Everyone agrees that in D&amp;D 3.5 wizards were OP in high levels etc. There are mechanics that are simply bad ideas.<br /> <br /> &quot;are run entirely by people&quot;<br /> <br /> And thats a problem, because it leads to arguments. Arguments at the table stop the game and interrupt the flow. The more fair and good the system is, the less arguments you're gonna have. That's one of the reasons i never got into Mage The Ascension/Awakening. Too much arguments over and over again about what can i do at this level, what is vulgar or not etc. Awakening did a better job in this regard, but still ends up in a lot of arguments. In this case, the rules are open on purpose, to allow free flow of magic, so arguments is a must.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12056-zulmaran","name":"Zulmaran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12056_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T15:10:50-08:00","id":1192415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zulmaran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192383#post1192383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its like saying that its the players fault if the video game your are playing has low security and allows hacks, because they shouldn't abuse it. No way, the fault is with the game, that didn't plan on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the difference between a video game hack, and a video game fan mod?<br /> <br /> Simple: There isn't a structural difference. The difference is the perception of intent. Video game hacks are &quot;bad&quot; because they violate the implicit social contract, esp. in multiplayer games, of winning based on skill at the game. Mods are &quot;good&quot; because they are perceived to improve the fun of the game; esp. in single player games where what mods you use or not don't impact anyone else's play.<br /> <br /> A video game &quot;bad hack&quot; is no different that people rules lawyering to avoid the spirit of the rules to farm Beats. It's a violation of social contract and expectations, rather than an inherent flaw in the game. If it wasn't making things unfun for someone (like all of us that are perfectly happy with the Beat rules and would prefer the proclamations of it being bad to be toned back to just being not to individuals' preferences), then it's like a mod: something you get to do to make the game yours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zulmaran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192406#post1192406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case, the rules are open on purpose, to allow free flow of magic, so arguments is a must.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been playing Ascension and Awakening (and similar things like Ars Magica) for over 20 year. I can count the number of table arguments about the magic rules I've been in on one hand.<br /> <br /> I have seen vast more table arguments in supposedly more tightly controlled systems precisely because they're more tightly controlled and edge cases are harder to adjudicate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192400#post1192400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of threadcapping (does it even apply to necroed ones like this?), I must exclaim,<br /> <br /> Not this again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... I have to admit I'm having flashbacks to the old &quot;grandma with a gun&quot; debates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T15:13:18-08:00","id":1192416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zulmaran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192406#post1192406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point Satchel, but even so, there are systems that are more open to abuse than others. This one is. Everyone agrees that in D&amp;D 3.5 wizards were OP in high levels etc. There are mechanics that are simply bad ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing: &quot;You get Beats from resolving Conditions&quot; is not geometrically-scaling class utility.<br /> <br /> &quot;Abusing&quot; the system means the ST has more things to throw at you because you're engaging with the hazards of the setting, divesting yourself of useful advantages, and otherwise living dangerously in a setting where a large part of why the supernatural is willfully ignored by mortals is because it is volatile and dangerous.<br /> <br /> The players who do not &quot;abuse&quot; the way Conditions are designed to work advance more slowly with the benefit being that their characters have more control over their actions and are less at risk of lasting damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And thats a problem, because it leads to arguments. Arguments at the table stop the game and interrupt the flow. The more fair and good the system is, the less arguments you're gonna have. </div> </div> </div>If your table is producing outcomes that are causing arguments, that is a thing you have to be on top of <i>regardless of how experience works</i>. Making sure everybody's expectations for the game are in line is your job, not the game's.<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;I would like you to either invest more in the things that make entering frenzy a bad idea, accept a reduced threshold or diminishing returns on getting Beats from entering frenzy, or not complain when I extend the consequences of your character entering frenzy all the time as part of the fiction&quot; is a thing the game is giving you credit for, because it is an inanimate object that already relies on you to enforce the rules within it as part of play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192353#post1192353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The beat system should encourage success and exceptional ideas and creativity, not just favoring the fuck ups.</div> </div> </div> </div>To get on top of this as well:<br /> <br /> The system already does this, too. It's literally the reason Promethean 2e has half of its Bestowments' effects translate to &quot;you get an exceptional success on three successes instead of five for this category of rolls&quot; \u2014 getting an exceptional success gives you a Condition, most commonly Inspired, which <i>lowers the exceptional success threshold for actions relating to that inspiration.</i><br /> <br /> You wanna advance quickly without being &quot;a fuck up&quot;? Hoard dice bonuses, route as much as you can through your areas of competence, and dedicate some portion of your resources to broadening the scope of &quot;your areas of competence&quot; \u2014 a practice which there are <i>multiple core Merits</i> to facilitate.<br /> <br /> The quick-and-dirty road to power being notionally viable in the short term is <i>part of the design</i>, especially for supernatural beings, but that by no means translates to &quot;the system only rewards you for bad decisions.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-06-2018, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T15:19:06-08:00","id":1192419,"title":"","content":"I guess we will have to agree to disagree, i really dont think its that simple and that this xp system, including conditions, is really, really bad! If it were not for the other benefits of this second edition, i would surely give it a pass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12056-zulmaran","name":"Zulmaran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12056_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T15:20:25-08:00","id":1192421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zulmaran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192419#post1192419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess we will have to agree to disagree</div> </div> </div> </div><i>You reraised a thread from two years ago to complain about this topic.</i><br /> <br /> Your opinion is your opinion and nobody is stopping you from having it, but if you have a problem with arguments it is generally a terrible idea to do something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T18:05:32-08:00","id":1192482,"title":"","content":"And... I'm always kinda surprised in these things when 1e Flaws are completely ignored. 1e Flaws worked exactly like 2e Persistent Conditions... 1e's XP system encouraged you to gain XP by having negative things happen to your character to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T18:08:40-08:00","id":1192484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zulmaran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192419#post1192419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess we will have to agree to disagree, i really dont think its that simple and that this xp system, including conditions, is really, really bad! If it were not for the other benefits of this second edition, i would surely give it a pass.</div> </div> </div> </div> You could have just as easily said &quot;I don't want to regard the opinions of others&quot; and saved us all some time here. If you raise a point of conversation about opinions without an intent to either make compelling cases that demonstrate comprehension* for people to change their minds or for you to be open to having your own mind changed, you might as well have remained silent.<br /> <br /> Don't a pick fight you have to then cower away from. The very least you could do is give credit that, while you don't think that would work for your table, at least you hadn't considered these perspectives before.<br /> <br /> *Should you find that your comprehension lacks, take time to consider it more fully and deeply and then resume the argumentation. Or at least lie about it.<br /> <br /> Point is, if you must complain about something, at least attempt some good faith discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T19:21:34-08:00","id":1192496,"title":"","content":"Not wanting to weight down on the discussion, since it appears it's closed, i just think this is relevant for anyone else qwho might read it and try to make their own opinion:<br /> <br /> V:tR2e, pag 104, Section &quot;Resisting Frenzy&quot;<br /> &quot;When a character enters frenzy, she gains a Beat. She can opt to turn a failure into a dramatic failure for a second Beat. <i><u><b>As with any Beats</b></u></i>, these Beats <u><i><b>only</b></i></u> come from <u><i><b>dramatic situations with consequences</b></i></u>&quot;<br /> <br /> (focus added by me)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T20:31:55-08:00","id":1192505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1192287#post1192287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the rules say that you get a beat every time you frenzy, so why NOT frenzy all the time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because not only is that Russian Roulette at its finest, you only get a Beat if the figurative gun actually fires (see post above this one).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You get a beat every time you go get a fix ( addicted ) instead of doing what the story teller says? Why not go wrack up the beats and deal with the story later? </div> </div> </div>Because a given Condition's &quot;Beat:&quot; clause only works once per session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Short term aspiration, I want to go get a big mac. Done. Beat. Now I want to eat it. Done. Beat. Now I want to drive to my sister's. Done. Beat. Now she wants to get a big mac, Done. Beat. </div> </div> </div>That's an awfully long lunch break considering you don't replace completed Aspirations until the end of the session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok So that's a little extreme, but within the rules </div> </div> </div>Incorrect, as you can see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T21:28:23-08:00","id":1192511,"title":"","content":"Just a note, the Beats from Conditions per X time isn't consistent between the books. Depending which CofD/2e texts you use, you can get different answers to that, which can mess with people's perceptions of the Beats system. Even so, there's still usually direct or practical reasons on why farming isn't as bad as some people are painting it just from those sorts of limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T08:31:34-08:00","id":1193140,"title":"","content":"I think the disagreement is more rooted in what could happen vs what actually happens.<br /> <br /> In my experience, the way Beats are given out is heavily rooted in GM fiat - which is how EXP works for most systems. The way Dramatic Failures work is heavily rooted in GM fiat, too. The thing is, in my experience, for the most part you'd prefer to avoid a Dramatic Failure. It can lead to some interesting places, but when you're dealing with an ST that doesn't pull their punches, you're basically agreeing to take on a big complication on top of an initial failure that's already put your character in a disadvantageous position. It's attractive, but it shouldn't be <i>that</i> attractive.<br /> <br /> Basically, I don't mind Beats being given as a consolation prize for getting the shit kicked out of your character.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't mind Beats being given as a carrot to make risky ideas more attractive. It's especially effective when it comes to social games; in my opinion, player agency is extremely important - but being able to offer Beats as an incentive while still retaining that player agency is fair play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T15:03:32-08:00","id":1193323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1193140#post1193140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the disagreement is more rooted in what could happen vs what actually happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely my view on this as well. That was my reference to the &quot;grandma with a rifle&quot; debates, which were an old thing from way back in early 1e nWoD when weapons acted as dice bonuses to attack rolls with people treating extreme edge cases as evidence of the system being broken over looking more at how things are generally used (not that in the end the developers didn't side with them and split attack and damage in 2e, but the debates got kinda ridiculous).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my experience, the way Beats are given out is heavily rooted in GM fiat... </div> </div> </div>Oddly, while I agree with a lot where you go with this, my experience is the opposite. The Beat system is much more slanted towards player agency than GM fiat because more Beats are generated by player choices than GM choices. The GM has input of course, the GM sets the stage and all that. But Aspirations are based on player choice, players choose to take dramatic failures for Beats, actively trying to farm Conditions takes far more player proactive effort to pull off, taking Beats for things like surrender in combat or social maneuvering is a player choice, etc.<br /> <br /> In the realms of player agency, the Beats method always feels more player oriented, because it's not the GM sitting around at the end of the session and assigning rewards as they desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T23:04:13-07:00","id":1195635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/563326-alternate-to-beats?p=1193323#post1193323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the realms of player agency, the Beats method always feels more player oriented, because it's not the GM sitting around at the end of the session and assigning rewards as they desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nicely put. I suppose it depends on the ST, because my experience is still pretty similar to being paid Beats as you go (accepting Dramatic Failures, resolving Conditions, getting hurt to a certain threshold, torpor, blood bonds) and being given Beats at the end of a scene for 'dramatic moments' ie successfully lying to a mentor, failing to lie to a mentor and being punished, befriending someone important, that sort of business - basically anything that creates an interesting development, progresses the plot, or just creates some interesting drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T13:40:38-07:00","id":1198829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my experience, the way Beats are given out is heavily rooted in GM fiat - which is how EXP works for most systems. </div> </div> </div>I don't see how a voluntary system can be rooted in the dreaded GM fiat. You CAN take a beat for a dramatic failure, if you as a player elect to do so. The ST can't force you to take it, you can simply just fail the roll and move on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is, in my experience, for the most part you'd prefer to avoid a Dramatic Failure. It can lead to some interesting places, but when you're dealing with an ST that doesn't pull their punches, you're basically agreeing to take on a big complication on top of an initial failure that's already put your character in a disadvantageous position. It's attractive, but it shouldn't be <i>that</i> attractive. </div> </div> </div>There is a lot to be said for the &quot;and then it gets worse&quot; approach to gaming - where the players relish the complications to the plot caused by things going completely off the rails, it can lead to some really fun in game moments. Even an ST who likes a down and dirty/things can get hairy on the turn of a dime style game - shouldn't let his players overuse the beat for dramatic failure mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I don't mind Beats being given as a carrot to make risky ideas more attractive. It's especially effective when it comes to social games; in my opinion, player agency is extremely important - but being able to offer Beats as an incentive while still retaining that player agency is fair play. </div> </div> </div>The way to do that fairly is to do it the way it's intended: the player decides to turn their failure into a dramatic failure in exchange for a beat and the storyteller determines the outcome of that dramatic failure - not the other way around. It's a barter system for the player to make a failed roll into something more dramatic and still eke out an award, not a tool for the storyteller to kick the shit out of his players.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}